    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Ndc67b33dcf414f408588e9bda6c8c8d0"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Systolic BP (mmHg)</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">This refers to the systolic blood pressure from the observation with the lowest mean arterial pressure (if mean arterial pressure has not been calculated, report the measurement with lowest systolic blood pressure).  For example, if the blood pressure is 120/85 mmHg, enter 120 in the section marked 'systolic BP'.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Enter the systolic blood pressure measured in millimetres of mercury (mmHg). Record the systolic blood pressure from the observation with the lowest mean arterial pressure (MAP) (if mean arterial pressure has not been calculated, report the measurement with lowest systolic blood pressure) that occurred between 00:00 to 24:00 on day of assessment.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
